# AUP served-bytes manifest -- version -> sha256 of the EXACT bytes served for that version.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (cp#396). AUP_VERSION is a LABEL and AUP_URL is a POINTER, and until now
# nothing tied them together. Either could move without the other, and on 2026-08-14 exactly that
# happened: AUP_URL was repointed at a different document while AUP_VERSION stayed 1.0.0, staged
# and waiting for the next unrelated deploy to swap the text behind four existing acceptances.
#
# The endpoint field GET /api/aup/current -> sha256 CANNOT catch this. It is computed at request
# time from the bytes it just fetched (src/index.ts, fetchAupSha256), so it always agrees with
# whatever it serves. It is a receipt of what was served, never a check on whether that was right.
# This file is the independent value it can be compared AGAINST.
#
# scripts/check-aup-pin.sh fetches AUP_URL at deploy time and refuses the deploy unless the bytes
# hash to the value recorded here for AUP_VERSION. That makes the label and the bytes unable to
# move apart: bump the version without re-pinning the URL and it fails; re-point the URL at
# different content under the same version and it fails.
#
# APPEND-ONLY. A line here describes bytes that a tenant may have accepted. Correcting a served
# version is a NEW version (see README.md), never an edit to its line.
#
# format: <version> <sha256>   (# comments and blank lines ignored)

